## Audit findings
| Area | Result | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| dir-fsync degradation | **Defect fixed** | EBADF was classified "unsupported" → would swallow a missing fsync caused by our own bug. Removed; EOPNOTSUPP/ENOTSUP compared separately (identical value 95 on Linux → duplicate case/map key would not compile). EINVAL/ENOSYS/EPERM stay tolerated (capability errors), EIO etc. stay fatal. TestDirSyncUnsupportedClassification |
| lifecycle renames | **Defect fixed** | All mail renames go through renameDurableLocked (spool.go:647, only os.Rename in spool.go:648) = rename + fsync dst dir + fsync src dir, also for cross-dir moves. Publish wrote the staging file with plain os.WriteFile → no content fsync before rename (failLocked already used writeFileDurableLocked). Publish now uses writeFileDurableLocked. TestPublishDurableWrite (new), TestPublishProcessLifecycle |
| cleanupStagingLocked | safe | Staging is per-repo (<clone>/mail/.tmp); every staging writer holds the same repo flock (<WorkDir>/<id>.lock): Publish locks at spool.go:305 before writing, writeFileDurableLocked only used by failLocked under the cycle lock, cleanup only via ensureLayoutLocked (spool.go:293) from Publish (333) and processLocked (356, lock from RunCycleForShips:244). Cross-repo: separate cloneDir+lock. Only removes crashed predecessors' files; never real spool content. Tests TestStagingCleanupRemovesLeftovers, TestFailedTransitionLeavesNoStagingFiles, TestRepositoryLockIsShared. Gap (low): no cross-process (exec) lock test |
| lock scope / multi-process | correct | flock per repo (git_sync.go:66,94), 60s timeout, used by Sync:109, Publish:305, RunCycleForShips:244; all git ops + transitions under it. Lock order wormhole→bus (processLocked→PostExternal takes bus lock); postAs calls publishRemote before taking the bus lock → no bus→wormhole nesting → no deadlock cycle. Observation (low): remote PostExternal under repo lock can make a second process hit its 60s lock timeout → error, fail-safe |
| failed/blocked/processed | correct | claim new→cur committed+pushed before import (481-491); processCurLocked re-asserts claim (524-530); cur→processed only after successful PostExternal (577-596); transient errors stay in cur/ (584); permanent errors typed via comms.IsPermanentPostExternalError → fail/ with durable .reason before the move (741-777) |
| retry classification | correct, noted | isNonFastForward (git_sync.go:416) string-matches git output; retry only then, fetch+rebase between attempts, bounded by push_retries, never force-push, conflict abort keeps local commits (rebaseLocked:387); LC_ALL=C enforced. Tests TestSyncUsesConfiguredPushRetries, TestPushRecoversFromConcurrentRemoteUpdate, TestGitCommandEnvForcesCLocale. Gap (low): string matching, not structural |
| error propagation | correct | pushLocked:427 → CommitAndPushLocked:576 → callers → errs → cycle result |
| workdir/remote/branch | correct | NewGitSync:62-70 (cloneDir/lockFile/stateDir), clone --branch cfg.Branch cfg.Remote:183, validateCloneDir:215-234 enforces remote+branch, ensureExcludes:238-266 excludes /.starfleet-state/ and /mail/.tmp/. Gap (low): mismatch branches untested |
| crash window before/after remote PostExternal | correct | claim durable before import; after import before cur→processed the replay hits the comms tombstone (source,externalID)→same CommsID, no second record, then processed/ is completed. Tests TestPostExternalCrashRecoveryImportsExactlyOnce, TestPostImportCrashRecoveryCompletesProcessedTransition, TestCrashRecoveryCommitsDirtyTransition, TestSuccessfulImportUnchanged. Inbound idempotency design (create-if-absent, hash check, per-recipient content check, crash-resumption tests) is sound |
| outbound crash window (Voyager/Discovery scope) | **finding, not modified** | postAs (commands.go:146) publishes remote first (172 → routing.go:213 → comms_transport.go:27 → messages.go:99 random ID → Spool.Publish push) and only then writes the local outbox record (commands.go:227) with plain os.WriteFile (no tmp/fsync/rename/dirsync). Crash in that window → remote holds w0-X, local has no record → reply correlation dangles; a retry creates a NEW random ID → duplicate remote message, both imported inbound. Severity medium. Design verdict: outbound exactly-once needs a pending-intent record (ID + payload hash) persisted atomically+durably BEFORE the transport call, marked sent after, and resumed on startup with the SAME ID — Spool.Publish is already idempotent for identical bytes and fails closed on differing bytes (spool.go:320-324), so no transport change is needed |

